{%- comment -%}
  "From our customers" — the voices wall. Port of components/home/testimonial-wall.tsx.

  Four vertical tracks on a plane tilted away from the reader, each carrying five
  reviews twice and travelling exactly one copy per cycle. The motion is pure CSS
  (.wl-voices-* in base.css), so this section costs no JavaScript at all — keep it
  that way.

  These are REAL Shopee reviews, reproduced verbatim. No rewriting, no tidying of
  the spelling, no translation. That is the whole reason this section is allowed to
  exist where a star rating is not: it quotes customers rather than manufacturing a
  score. They are in Indonesian while the rest of the site is English, and that is
  the point — translating a quotation turns it into a paraphrase. Never edit one,
  and never add a review that did not come from the store.

  The geometry below was measured against the design, not eyeballed:
    - Perspective stays long (2200px). The tracks are ~2,700px tall; at the
      reference component's 300px their far ends cross the camera plane and most
      of the reviews never appear on screen.
    - The offsets desynchronise the tracks. A reversed track rests at -50% at
      t=0, so without one it runs out of content before the bottom of the stage.
    - Durations are four different lengths. Equal ones lock into step within
      seconds and the wall reads as a single sliding block.

  TWO BLOCK TYPES, and the split is the point.

  `review` is a card in the moving wall. `fit` lifts the body measurement a
  review already states — "BB 38/155", "TB 167 cm, BB 60" — out of 14px type on a
  tilted, moving plane and sets it at display size above the stage. Fit against a
  stated body is the purchase decision on this site (PRODUCT.md), and the inside
  of a slowly rotating 3D wall is the least readable place it could be. Every
  `fit` value is a verbatim substring of a review below, copied not retyped:
  seven of the twenty reviews state a measurement, and those seven are the seven
  blocks. No piece is attached to any of them — only some reviewers name one, and
  attaching one to the rest would invent an association the customer never made.
  The size line is optional for the same reason. The alias is the reviewer's own.
  The tracks slice the `review` blocks only, so adding a `fit` block cannot
  shorten a column.

  This is also the site's second reachable use of --text-display. One display
  moment per band: the heading deliberately stays at text-h1, because two
  display-scale objects 40px apart cancel each other out.

  The band's ground is espresso — bg-invert, i.e. --wl-taupe-900, which is one of
  the brand's own five named colourways and its darkest garment colour. A token
  used where it was not used before, not a new one. The cards stay cream, and the
  four stage fades are painted from-invert to match the ground they lie on. BOTH
  halves matter: cream cards on a cream band vanish, and a fade in any colour but
  the surface underneath draws the visible rectangle this effect always risks. If
  the band's ground ever moves, bg-invert here and from-invert on the four fades
  move together. The card's old border-brand/13 edge is gone with the white shell
  that needed it — cream on espresso is its own edge.

  Do NOT wrap this section in anything that animates opacity. That makes the
  wrapper a stacking context, which flattens preserve-3d — the plane's
  translateZ(-100px) stops pushing cards behind the fades and the top of the wall
  ends in a hard edge. It is why app/page.tsx leaves it unwrapped.

  prefers-reduced-motion does not merely pause this: a stopped wall holds most of
  its reviews outside a stage that clips at 560px. It flattens to a plain grid
  instead (base.css) — on espresso that grid reads as a deliberate dark editorial
  panel rather than a carousel somebody stopped. Below md the same thing happens
  on its side, and there the four fades are hidden entirely, so the cards go
  cream-on-espresso with nothing over them: more contrast on a phone, not less.

  Keep the review count a multiple of four, or the last column runs short.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign reviews = section.blocks | where: 'type', 'review'
  assign fits = section.blocks | where: 'type', 'fit'
  assign durations = 'var(--duration-voices-a),var(--duration-voices-b),var(--duration-voices-c),var(--duration-voices-d)' | split: ','
  assign offsets = '380px,300px,440px,340px' | split: ','
-%}

{%- if section.blocks.size > 0 -%}
  <section aria-labelledby="voices-heading" class="flex flex-col gap-10 bg-invert py-section">
    <div class="mx-auto w-full max-w-content px-gutter flex flex-col items-center gap-3">
      <h2 id="voices-heading" class="text-center text-h1 leading-h1 text-ink-invert">
        {% render 'copy', value: section.settings.heading, label: 'heading' %}
      </h2>
      {%- comment -%}
        The same short rule that sits under New arrivals. Decorative, so a div
        rather than an <hr>: there is no section break here. Taupe-200 rather
        than brand taupe: the rule is decorative, so nothing obliges it to any
        ratio, but brand taupe on espresso measures 3.91:1 against taupe-200's
        11.49:1 and at 3px tall the darker one reads as a smudge.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <div aria-hidden="true" class="h-0.75 w-16 rounded-pill bg-ink-invert-muted"></div>
    </div>

    {%- if fits.size > 0 -%}
      {%- comment -%}
        The measurements, quoted. figure/blockquote/figcaption because each one
        IS a quotation with a named source — the same markup the cards use, at
        the size the number deserves. data-numeric gives them tabular figures so
        the column of measurements does not wobble.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <ul role="list" class="mx-auto grid w-full max-w-content grid-cols-1 gap-x-8 gap-y-10 px-gutter sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3">
        {%- for block in fits -%}
          <li>
            <figure class="flex flex-col gap-2">
              <blockquote data-numeric class="font-display text-display leading-display tracking-display text-ink-invert">
                {% render 'copy', value: block.settings.measure, label: 'measurement' %}
              </blockquote>
              <figcaption class="flex flex-wrap items-baseline gap-x-3 gap-y-1 text-caption leading-snug text-ink-invert-muted">
                {%- if block.settings.size != blank -%}
                  <span class="text-ink-invert">{{ block.settings.size }}</span>
                {%- endif -%}
                <span>{{ block.settings.user }}</span>
              </figcaption>
            </figure>
          </li>
        {%- endfor -%}
      </ul>
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- if reviews.size > 0 -%}
      {%- comment -%}
        Full-bleed through a normal full-width parent, never 100vw — that includes
        the scrollbar gutter and puts 8px of horizontal scroll on the page.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <div class="wl-voices-stage wl-rail relative flex h-140 w-full items-center justify-center overflow-hidden [perspective:2200px]">
        <div class="wl-voices-plane flex items-start gap-6 [transform-style:preserve-3d]">
          {%- for column in (0..3) -%}
            {%- liquid
              assign slice_size = reviews.size | divided_by: 4
              assign start = column | times: slice_size
              assign finish = start | plus: slice_size | minus: 1
              assign reverse = false
              if column == 1 or column == 3
                assign reverse = true
              endif
            -%}
            <div
              class="wl-voices-track"
              {% if reverse %}data-reverse{% endif %}
              style="--voices-duration:{{ durations[column] }};--voices-offset:{{ offsets[column] }}"
            >
              {%- comment -%}
                Two copies, so -50% lands on an identical frame. The trailing
                padding is what makes that land on the gap, not mid-card.
              {%- endcomment -%}
              {%- for copy in (0..1) -%}
                <div {% if copy == 1 %}aria-hidden="true"{% endif %} class="flex flex-col gap-6 pb-6">
                  {%- for i in (start..finish) -%}
                    {%- assign block = reviews[i] -%}
                    {%- if block -%}
                      {%- comment -%}
                        Locked to 300x250 with the quote clamped, per the design's
                        "same size for all": ragged cards on a tilted plane read as
                        a mistake rather than a wall.
                      {%- endcomment -%}
                      <figure class="flex h-62.5 w-75 shrink-0 flex-col gap-3.5 overflow-hidden bg-canvas p-6">
                        <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
                          <span aria-hidden="true" class="flex size-9 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-pill bg-avatar font-display text-small text-on-avatar">
                            {{ block.settings.user | slice: 0 | upcase }}
                          </span>
                          <figcaption class="text-caption tracking-[0.02em] text-ink">{{ block.settings.user }}</figcaption>
                        </div>
                        <blockquote class="line-clamp-6 text-caption leading-snug text-ink-body">
                          {{ block.settings.body }}
                        </blockquote>
                      </figure>
                    {%- endif -%}
                  {%- endfor -%}
                </div>
              {%- endfor -%}
            </div>
          {%- endfor -%}
        </div>

        {%- comment -%}
          The fades sit on the stage, not inside the transformed stack — inside,
          they inherit the tilt and stop covering the edges they exist to hide.
          from-invert, because the ground under them is the espresso band.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <div aria-hidden="true" class="pointer-events-none absolute inset-x-0 top-0 hidden h-[42%] md:block motion-reduce:md:hidden bg-linear-to-b from-invert from-[16%] to-transparent"></div>
        <div aria-hidden="true" class="pointer-events-none absolute inset-x-0 bottom-0 hidden h-[42%] md:block motion-reduce:md:hidden bg-linear-to-t from-invert from-[16%] to-transparent"></div>
        <div aria-hidden="true" class="pointer-events-none absolute inset-y-0 left-0 hidden w-[30%] md:block motion-reduce:md:hidden bg-linear-to-r from-invert from-[24%] to-transparent"></div>
        <div aria-hidden="true" class="pointer-events-none absolute inset-y-0 right-0 hidden w-[30%] md:block motion-reduce:md:hidden bg-linear-to-l from-invert from-[24%] to-transparent"></div>
      </div>
    {%- endif -%}
  </section>
{%- endif -%}

{% schema %}
